            <ArticleTitle>Norovirus GII.17 Associated with a Foodborne Acute Gastroenteritis Outbreak in Brazil, 2016.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s12560-017-9326-0</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Foodborne transmission gastroenteritis (AGE) outbreak occurred during a celebration lunch in July, 2016, Brazil. All stool samples tested were positive for noroviruses (NoV) and phylogenetic analysis revealed that strains were genetically close to GII.17 Kawasaki_2014. These findings indicated circulation of NoV GII.17 Kawasaki_2014 in the Brazilian population, associated with AGE outbreak.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
